&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are Ocado Group,&lt;/strong&gt; and we&#39;re bringing world-class automation to online grocery. Our Ocado Smart Platform (OSP) combines cutting-edge robotics, AI, and IoT within our advanced CFCs (Customer Fulfilment Centres). We&#39;ve mastered the single pick, transforming online delivery for our global partners. Join us and be part of a team pushing the boundaries of retail technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Senior Finance Business Partner role supports our Operations organisation across three key areas: capital expenditure for selected Customer Fulfilment Centre projects, the Real Estate P&amp;amp;L (covering UK and European office and development centre running costs), and the direct operating costs and capital investment for our Ocado Mobile Robot System (OMRS) products, Chuck and Porter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted finance lead—providing constructive challenge and practical guidance to help stakeholders make sound decisions through accurate budgets, clear forecasts, period-end reporting, and targeted ad hoc analysis. Working closely with the wider finance team, you will establish clear visibility over the OMRS cost base to help drive contribution margin across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who thrives in a fast-evolving environment, excels at balancing competing priorities, and builds strong relationships across all levels of seniority. You will also take the initiative to streamline reporting—leveraging AI and automation tools where appropriate to cut down manual work and free up time for high-value commercial analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
